{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Verified -1 on patch set 1 — fixed in patch set 2, and the fake was the real story\n\nCI run 30984771071 failed 4 of 15 jobs: the same two tests on each of the four pytest legs.\nEvery other job (lint, typecheck, module-size gate, etc.) passed.\n\n    tests/interfaces/test_metrics_polyglot.py::test_metrics_cli_reports_polyglot_code_health_values[python-src/main.py]\n    tests/interfaces/test_metrics_polyglot.py::test_metrics_cli_reports_polyglot_code_health_values[typescript-src/main.ts]\n    KeyError: 'value'\n\n### The mechanism was NOT the AC2 guard\n\nThe obvious reading is that the AC2 empty-map guard fired. It did not. Reproduced locally and\nread the actual reason off the metric document rather than inferring it:\n\n    module_size_distribution -> {\"unavailable\": {\"reason\":\n      \"scc produced invalid JSON: file entry has invalid location or line count\", ...}}\n\nThat is the AC4 change, not AC2. The fixture's fake `scc` emitted `{\"Location\": ..., \"Code\": n}`;\nthe adapter now reads `Lines`, gets `None`, and `_parse_files` raises its existing ValueError,\nwhich surfaces through the pre-existing invalid-JSON path. The distinction matters: a fix that\nonly made the stub argv-faithful (gating on `--by-file`) without also switching its emitted\nfield to `Lines` would have left the test RED. There were two independent fidelity gaps.\n\n### What the stub actually did\n\n`tests/interfaces/metrics_polyglot_support.py::fake_analyzer_bin` wrote an `scc` stand-in that\nwalked the scan root and emitted a per-file entry for every file, UNCONDITIONALLY — it never\nlooked at its own argv. Real scc only populates `Files` when `--by-file` is passed; without it\nevery language group carries an empty list. So the stub was strictly MORE PERMISSIVE than the\ntool it stands in for, and that is precisely why this test could not catch the missing\n`--by-file` in the first place. The fake hid the bug it existed to detect.\n\n### The fix: make the fake model the tool\n\nThe stub is now argv-faithful. Verified directly against all four branches:\n\n    --format json                                -> []              (summary mode, as real scc)\n    --by-file --format json                      -> main.py, main.ts, notes.txt\n    --by-file --include-ext py --format json     -> main.py\n    --by-file --include-ext py,ts --format json  -> main.py, main.ts\n\nIt also emits BOTH `Lines` and `Code` with genuinely different values (`main.py` -> Lines 3,\nCode 2), modelling real scc's distinction rather than collapsing them.\n\nThis matches the real-scc behaviour measured at the top of this ticket exactly: `scc --format\njson src/rebar` yields empty `Files`, `scc --by-file` yields 729 entries.\n\n### It is now a genuine regression guard for this ticket\n\nConfirmed by mutation, not assumed: drop `--by-file` from the adapter and the polyglot test\ngoes RED (`KeyError: 'value'`, because the adapter correctly reports unavailable), then passes\nagain when restored. Anyone who removes the flag in future is now caught by an interface test\nas well as by the unit oracle. That is a strictly better outcome than merely getting CI green.\n\n### include_extensions ruled out explicitly, not assumed\n\nBoth fixtures (`tests/fixtures/metrics_polyglot/{python,typescript}/pyproject.toml`) set only\n`enabled`, `scan_roots = [\"src\"]` and `size_cap = 800`. Neither sets `include_extensions`, so it\ndefaults to `[]` and no `--include-ext` is emitted. The TypeScript leg was never being narrowed\nto `py`; it failed for the same `Lines`/`Code` reason as the Python leg. Both now pass.\n\n### Status\n\nPatch set 2 pushed to the SAME change (Gerrit reported `updated: 1`, and the stale `Verified -1`\nwas auto-removed). Change-Id `I9155...80cb` preserved — note the first `--amend` regenerated it\nand it had to be restored explicitly, or this would have forked a second change.\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1425 — awaiting fresh Verified + LLM-Review.\n`make lint` clean, `make typecheck` clean, polyglot tests 4 passed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785916536019096001,"uuid":"47e76a44-b531-46ab-95dd-f606ae793b12"}